<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes" ?>
<!--
    No <exclude> group here, deliberately, and adding one would be actively harmful.

    Auto-run's whole job is to keep a movement input alive while nothing is held, and both
    AddActiveInputExcludes and RemoveActiveInputExcludes end in GetUApi().UpdateControls() - "call
    this on each change of exclusion" - which rebuilds the whole control state and drops the HELD
    state of every input, UATurbo included. See Extra/Map/Data/Inputs.xml for the longer version of
    that story.

    Nothing is suppressed either. The four movement inputs are read here only to CANCEL auto-run;
    UAInput.Supress must never be pointed at a movement key, because its contract is "supress press
    event for next frame while not pressed ATM - otherwise until release".
-->
<modded_inputs>
    <inputs>
        <actions>
            <!-- loc= takes a BARE stringtable key with no leading '#'. Keys live in this
                 addon's own stringtable.csv - auto-run must not reference a STR_BR_* key. -->
            <input name="UAVigridAutoRunToggle" loc="STR_AUTORUN_KEYBIND_TOGGLE" />
        </actions>

        <sorting name="vigridautorun" loc="STR_AUTORUN_KEYBIND_CATEGORY">
            <input name="UAVigridAutoRunToggle" />
        </sorting>
    </inputs>
    <preset>
        <!--
            Z, not X. kX is vanilla UAToggleWeapons (change firearm fire mode, and it also pokes the
            zeroing HUD - preset_keymouseprimary.xml:193, consumed at missiongameplay.c:551), so a
            bind there fires twice on every press. kZ's only vanilla binding is UAMoveDown, which
            sits under the preset's "DEBUG SPECIFIC / Freefly Camera" block and is unreachable in
            normal gameplay - which is also why DayZ-Expansion's own auto-run defaulted to it, so
            players coming off Expansion keep their muscle memory.

            Free letters are nearly exhausted: K, O and P are the only ones vanilla leaves unbound,
            and Map has taken K, Party has taken P. Community-Online-Tools is the one to check if a
            bind ever does two things at once - its Inputs.xml is what collided with Party's Y.
        -->
        <input name="UAVigridAutoRunToggle">
            <btn name="kZ" />
        </input>
    </preset>
</modded_inputs>
